#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'TXT'
Git Bash Linux-Like Environment
===============================

Common commands already supplied by Git Bash:
  ls cd pwd mkdir rmdir rm cp mv touch cat echo clear
  grep sed awk find sort uniq head tail wc cut xargs
  chmod ln tar gzip gunzip ssh scp sftp curl vim
  ps kill which env export history bash sh git

Added Linux-style compatibility commands:
  apt / apt-get   WinGet-backed package management
  man             Show a command's --help output in less
  ifconfig        Windows network information
  ip              Limited: ip addr, ip link, ip route
  free            Memory summary
  open            Open a file/folder with Windows
  snap            Explains why Snap requires real Linux/WSL

Convenience aliases:
  ll la l
  .. ... ....
  cls / c
  home

Installed automatically when WinGet is available:
  nano
  wget
  jq

Package examples:
  apt update
  apt search python
  apt install make
  apt install ripgrep
  apt remove jq

Useful diagnostics:
  which <command>
  type <command>
  echo $PATH
  refreshpath
  linux-check

This environment is Git Bash on Windows, not a Linux kernel. Commands such as
systemctl, snap packages, kernel modules, /dev hardware behavior, and Linux
service management require WSL or a real Linux machine.
TXT
